  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Smart Garden. Education</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The &quot;Smart garden. Education&quot; project, a continuation of &quot;Smart Garden&quot; and &quot;Smart Garden. Microgreens,&quot; aims to enhance economic success and development among Ukrainian schoolchildren by providing knowledge and practical experience in agronomy, project management, accounting, marketing, sales, and entrepreneurship.The project enables the online and off-line training of up to 1000 children from the last years of school (13 years old +); who will receive the necessary support to identify and to develop their own agri-business ideas using the school platform system and foresee but project modules. In addition, the project aims to reach 3,000 school children for digital training on agriculture and entrepreneurship. During implementation, the local representatives of the Dutch companies and other local private partners actively participate in the format of guest lectures, seminars, on-line and off-line meetings not only in the agronomic field, but also in business education.The project has a positive impact on:SDG 8: Inclusive and sustainable economic growth. SDG 4: Quality education. SDG 2: No hunger.</narrative>
  </description>
